{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered while proving bug `5931-78a3-95d2-44cd` (marker dropped by truncation). The\nCloud outbound comment path fits the SAME body with TWO different rules, so the\nbody-equality dedup can never match for an over-length comment.\n\n- **Differ / comparison key** — `outbound_comments._diff_comments` computes\n  `sanitizer.fit_comment(body)`. Cloud's `_JiraSanitizer.fit_comment`\n  (`adapters/jira/backend.py:152-154`) is `comment_limits.truncate_comment_body`, a\n  PLAIN-CHARACTER cap at `_JIRA_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS = 32767`.\n- **Send path** — `adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.add_comment` fits with\n  `AdfCodec.fit_outbound` -> `adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit`, which measures the SERIALIZED\n  ADF against `_ADF_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT = 32000`.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\nDriving both with a 40,000-char body (worktree `fix-illadopsis-marker`, repo venv):\n\n```\ncompare key len:      32767\nlanded jira key len:  31887\nBODY-EQUALITY SECONDARY SKIP HITS (today): False\n```\n\nThe two keys can never be equal for any over-length comment.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`emersed-specific-mutt` made the ID-based skip (`binding_store.is_comment_mapped` /\n`jira_comment_id`) PRIMARY, so this is the belt-and-suspenders layer — but that layer is\nexactly the guard against a lost map write (a crash between `add_comment` and\n`record_comment_id`). For over-length comments it is structurally dead, so a lost map\nwrite re-posts every pass. `comment_limits.py`'s own docstring states the convergence\nrequirement this violates: \"If the two paths used different truncation logic they could\nnever agree on the landed body, and the loop would persist.\"\n\nNot fixed under 5931 — that bug's fix is confined to preserving the marker and does not\nchange any comparison key. This divergence predates it and is unchanged by it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The differ's comment comparison key and the Cloud send path apply the identical fit.\n- [ ] A test drives both and asserts the landed body equals the comparison key for an\n      over-length comment (RED on current code).","id":"e339-9709-15fe-419a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud comment dedup key is fitted at 32767 while the send path fits at the 32000 ADF limit"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787293597347835001,"uuid":"8aafa949-85c3-49dc-8c23-04db72ff03c6"}